From 2a63bfda3aa14a4ab723824b5e8752e53a562ac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: idiazraz <100824525+idiazraz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] airoha: en7523: add Skyworth GN630V

Skyworth GN630V GPON ONT: Airoha AN7529CT (EN7523 family, 2x Cortex-A53
in AArch32), 512 MB DDR, 256 MiB FORESEE F35SQB002G SPI-NAND, MT7916
Wi-Fi, 4x GbE through the internal MT7530. Dual-image vendor U-Boot.

Flash layout and boot:
- the vendor U-Boot boots a bank (A at 0xc0000, B at 0x20c0000, 32 MiB
  each) as an HDR2 header + FIT; get_tclinux_imginfo() reads only the
  first 0x800 bytes of the FIT and looks up /images/fdt@1, kernel@1 and
  filesystem@1 by name. tclinux-fit.sh builds the FIT in stock order and
  names, a copy of econet's tclinux-trx.sh wraps it (rootfs at +6 MiB)
- each bank: 6 MiB kernel, 16 MiB squashfs, 10 MiB UBI overlay; the
  partition order makes the root= U-Boot passes (mtdblock3 for A,
  mtdblock6 for B) the squashfs of the bank it booted
- sysupgrade and preinit only ever write the bank they booted from, so
  the other bank keeps stock as the fallback; U-Boot also falls back by
  itself when a bank fails to parse
- alphawrt-bootbank switches the U-Boot bootflag (one byte at 0xdfc0000)
- no devtmpfs: UBI nodes are created from sysfs in preinit and stage2
- tclinux-factory.bin installs from the stock web UI: the page wants
  "tclinux" in the file name, the firmware checks the HDR2 magic, CRC
  and model, and crashes on an empty HDR2 customer version

Board:
- MAC from the U-Boot env ethaddr (mac-base nvmem cell), +4 for Wi-Fi
- MT7916 EEPROM from reservearea 0x4c000
- LEDs for power, PON and internet; all four ports on LAN
- backport mainline 1d9d5f5a5040 for F35SQB002G support
- enable DSA for the MT7530 switch; restore upstream's airoha target
  Makefile (the GPIO LED/key drivers are not built in)

Not yet: GPON/OMCI, Wi-Fi AP defaults, buttons and the remaining LEDs.
